 funds customs the  marketplace and to a lesser extent  tobacco and counterfeit items we are  mainly an investigative body so we  investigate we try to find out how  things are happened what has happened if  there is a fraud or crime or nothing and  then we recommend the actions that is we  are not a sanctioning body the sanctions  like disciplinary financial or judicial  are taken by the competent authority  through their own procedures in 2014 all  as recommendations aim to recover 900  million euros that's just over half a  percent of the in use total budget for  that year smugglers are becoming  increasingly inventive this roll of  paper is stuffed full of smuggled  cigarettes one ships container can hold  about 10 million cigarettes hidden in  rules like this and that represents in  terms of lost revenue from tanks and  import duty around two and a half  million euros but do Europe's  authorities follow the advice of the  length mostly not always there is an  autonomy of these bodies to take  measures when it comes to the judicial  authorities which are you know  independent and there are hundreds of  them in Europe the results are quite  varied over the years and depending also  on the countries and on the cases whilst  when it comes to the new institutions  there is more consistency and more  our recommendation are followed in  addition to investigations of fraud  corruption and any illegal activity  related to EU funds Olaf is also  responsible for detecting serious  offenses committed by personnel of the  European Union be the officials  politicians elected as M EPS or  Commissioners and finally Olaf obviously  contributes to the development of  Europe's anti-fraud policy
 

